CHAPTER VIII
CHILD-FRIENDLY REGENCY
Article 76
(1) To guarantee the fulfillment of children's rights to live, grow, develop, and participate optimally in accordance with human dignity and to receive protection from violence and discrimination, concrete integrated efforts are needed among the local government, the community, and the business sector through the development of a Child-Friendly Regency.
(2) The implementation of a Child-Friendly Regency by the Regency Government is intended to:
a. Guarantee the fulfillment of children's rights to live, grow, develop and participate optimally in accordance with human dignity, for the realization of quality children with noble character and prosperity;
b. Guarantee the fulfillment of children's rights in creating a sense of security, a friendly and amicable atmosphere;
c. Protect children from the threat of social problems in their lives;
d. Develop the potential, talents and creativity of children;
e. Optimize the role and function of the family as the first educational base for children; and
f. Build Regency facilities and infrastructure capable of meeting the basic needs of children to grow and develop optimally.

