Article 85
(1) The Regional Head has the authority to conduct guidance and supervision over the Protection of Women and Children.
(2) The form of guidance as referred to in paragraph (1) may include:
a. providing socialization to the community and children's groups regarding the concept of a Child-Friendly Regency and children's rights;
b. providing books, leaflets, brochures regarding child protection, reproductive health, the dangers of Sexually Transmitted Diseases and Narcotics and other Addictive Substances (NAPZA), and distributing them to the community;
c. providing training related to child care/education, counseling principles, and basic psychology to communities participating in efforts to organize early childhood education, the development of Toddler Family Development Groups (BKB), the implementation of integrated child protection services, and other similar activities related to fulfilling children's needs;
d. facilitating the organization of children's forums and components of children's socio-cultural groups;
e. facilitating the growth and development of centers or platforms for information and counseling services for adolescents;
f. providing awards to the community, both individuals and groups or community organizations that are deemed to have carried out child protection efforts well.
(3) Supervision as referred to in paragraph (1) may include monitoring and evaluation activities of the Protection of Women and Children carried out by child protection service providers/implementers.
(4) The authority as referred to in paragraph (1) may be delegated to the Head of Women's Empowerment and Family Planning and/or other officials within the Regional Government in accordance with their respective duties and functions.

